      "problem": "Consider the following geometric sequence:\n\n$$\n243,\\,-162,\\,108,\\,-72,\\,…\n$$\n\nThe common ratio of this geometric sequence is{{field-1}}.",
      "worked_solution": "The common ratio $r$ of a geometric sequence is the constant we multiply by to get to the next term. In other words, it is the ratio of consecutive terms.\n\nTherefore, the common ratio for our sequence is\n\n$$\nr=\\frac{{a}_{2}}{{a}_{1}}=\\frac{(-162)}{243}=-\\frac{2}{3}.\n$$",
